<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>MPE Noise Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To add noise to our observation we define</p>
<table id="A3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}=x+\epsilon,\hskip 10.00002pt\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,(k\cdot\sigma_{x})^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}=x+\epsilon,\hskip 10.00002pt\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,(k\cdot\sigma_{x})^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Under this formulation, the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) in terms of variance is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SNR}_{\text{power}}=\frac{\sigma_{x}^{2}}{(k\cdot\sigma_{x})^{2}}=\frac{1}{k^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>power</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SNR}_{\text{power}}=\frac{\sigma_{x}^{2}}{(k\cdot\sigma_{x})^{2}}=\frac{1}{k^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">At the maximum scale <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, the SNR is <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{:}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{:}1</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning signal variance is four times noise variance.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Diagnostic Measures</h2>

<figure id="A4.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 15</span>. </span><span id="A4.T15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Normalised diagnostic metrics (mean with 95% stratified bootstrap CI). Values exceeding the permutation-null baseline are <span id="A4.T15.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span>. For FF policies, <math id="A4.T15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{HAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>HAR</mi><mi>norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{HAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math> uses an observation-history window and <math id="A4.T15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PIF}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>PIF</mi><mi>norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PIF}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A4.T15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DAI}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>DAI</mi><mi>norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DAI}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math> use an observation-action history window; for RNN policies these use the hidden state. <math id="A4.T15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AA}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>AA</mi><mi>norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AA}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math> is architecture-independent. <sup id="A4.T15.4.2" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A4.T15.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup>One or more metrics are undefined due to degenerate action entropy.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T15.15" class="ltx_tabular">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T15.15.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><span id="A4.T15.15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Domain</span></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><span id="A4.T15.15.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Environment</span></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><span id="A4.T15.15.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Algorithm</span></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><math id="A4.T15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{OAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">OAR</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{OAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><math id="A4.T15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{HAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">HAR</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{HAR}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><math id="A4.T15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PIF}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">PIF</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PIF}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><math id="A4.T15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AA}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">AA</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AA}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T15.15.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;"><math id="A4.T15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DAI}^{\mathrm{norm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">DAI</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">norm</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DAI}^{\mathrm{norm}}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T15.15.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T15.15.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.2pt 2.0pt;" rowspan="12"><span id="A4.T15.15.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">MPE</span></td>
